
# Cloudflare Workers DOM: the SAME in-memory server DOM as node. SSR is pure -- build an element
# tree, mutate it, serialize it to HTML -- with no platform dependency, so the Worker target reuses
# the node impl wholesale. Only the HTTP transport (http/native/cloudflare) and asset serving
# (zone/native/cloudflare) differ per env; the DOM does not. Re-exports the node in-memory dom, whose
# serializer and document shell (../node/html.tree) are pure string building (its filesystem reads, the
# prod asset manifest and the build id, degrade to dev asset names on a Worker, which the transport still serves).

bear @term/site/dom/native/node/dom
